WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410
Drop a steel nail
into a bowl of water,

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.890
and it sinks straight to the bottom.

3
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.790
Yet a steel ship weighing many
thousands of tonnes floats on

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.150
the sea, loaded with cargo.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.070
Both are made of steel.

6
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.550
So why does the tiny nail sink
while the giant ship floats?

7
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.590
In this mission, you'll find
out why the pressure in a liquid

8
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.660
gets bigger the deeper you go.

9
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.970
You'll meet upthrust, the
upward push from a fluid,

10
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.150
and work out when an object
floats and when it sinks.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.020
Your mission: find out why
a steel ship can float.
